module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneratedColimit.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.HomogeneousTwist
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.LaurentChartDictionary

/-!
# Differentials of functions pulled back from the base of the line bundle

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes, `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module and `L^⋆ ⟶ X` the
complement of the zero section of the associated line bundle. For a pair of affine opens
`W ≤ U` of `X`, the relative de Rham differential on `L^⋆` of a function pulled back from `W` is
a `Γ(X, W)`-combination of restrictions of differentials of functions pulled back from `U`.

This is the one step the expansion of a homogeneous form over a smaller affine open does not
reach on its own. Writing a section of `L^{⊗ j}` over `W` through restrictions from `U` and
applying the Leibniz rule leaves the differential of a function pulled back from `W`, and that
is again a degree-zero one-form over `π⁻¹W` — the same shape the expansion started from, so the
recursion does not descend. What breaks it is that the differential of a pulled-back function
comes from a differential on `X`, where `Ω_{X/S}` is quasi-coherent and the chart dictionary
applies: the combination can be found on `X` and then pushed forward.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferentialsPushHom`: the adjoint
  `Ω_{X/S} ⟶ π_* Ω_{L^⋆/S}` of the canonical map of Tag 01UV attached to the square of the
  projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X`, `f` and `Situation.laurentToBase`. Only this instance of the adjoint is
  built; the general one is not.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.gradedAmbient` and `Situation.homogeneousSet`: the pushed-forward
  forms read at the `X.Modules` spelling, and the homogeneous forms of a given degree over an
  affine open as a set of its sections.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top_of_isAffineOpen`: **the
  sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an affine open of `X` are generated by the differentials of the
  functions there**, with no hypothesis relating the open to an affine open of `S`. The version
  in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.LaurentChartDictionary` carries that
  hypothesis, which no affine open of an arbitrary `X` over `S` need satisfy.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_image_range_universalDSections_eq_top`: **over a nested pair
  of affine charts the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over the smaller one are spanned by the restrictions
  of the differentials of the functions on the bigger one.**
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferentialsPushHom_d`: **the adjoint carries the
  differential of a function on `X` to the differential of its pullback to `L^⋆`.**
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span` and
  `Situation.laurentDifferential_pullback_mem_span`: **the differential of a function pulled back
  from the smaller chart is a `Γ(X, W)`-combination of restrictions of differentials of functions
  pulled back from the bigger one**, in `π_* Ω_{L^⋆/S}` and then as a one-form.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.gradedAmbient_presheaf_map` and
  `Situation.homogeneousSet_image_subset`, `Situation.span_homogeneousSet_image_le`: the
  restriction map of the re-seated pushforward is the inverse-image restriction of the forms, on
  the nose; hence restrictions of homogeneous forms are homogeneous, and one of the two
  inclusions a compatible family of submodules asks for.

## Implementation notes

`Situation.laurentFormsPushforward` is declared with type `SheafOfModules D.X.ringCatSheaf`. At
that spelling `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.presheaf` does not project — the error is
`Invalid field 'presheaf'` — and the `Module` instances of the `Γ(·, ·)` notation are not found,
so `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible` cannot be *stated* against it.
`Situation.gradedAmbient` is the same object with its type given as `D.X.Modules`, which it is by
definition, and at that spelling `GabberColimit.isCompatible_span` applies unchanged. This is the
same re-seating that `LaurentChartDictionary` performs for the degree-one generator, at the level
of the ambient module rather than of a morphism.

What makes the restriction half free is that
`(Situation.gradedAmbient p).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op` and
`(D.laurentFormsAlgebra.piece p).val.map (D.laurentPreimageHom h).op` are the same map by `rfl`,
so `Situation.isHomogeneousLaurentForm_map` — which is stated at the second spelling — is an
inclusion of generating sets with nothing in between.

`Situation.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span` is stated through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap` of the adjoint rather than through its
`Hom.app` so that `Γ(X, W)`-linearity is available: the span is taken over `Γ(X, W)`, and the
scalar step of the induction over `Submodule.span` is `map_smul`.
`Situation.laurentDifferentialsPushHom_d` is what says which elements those are.

## Dropping the affine open of `S`

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.LaurentChartDictionary` needs the affine open
`U` of `X` to map into an affine open of `S`, because it goes through the chart dictionary, which
identifies `Γ(Ω_{X/S}, U)` with the Kähler differentials of a ring map. An arbitrary affine open
of `X` need not map into an affine open of `S`, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible` quantifies over *all* nested pairs of
affine opens of `X`, so that version does not reach the compatibility condition. What replaces it
is the basic-open argument: `U` is covered by basic opens which do map into an affine open of `S`,
over each of those the differentials of the functions generate, and a function on a basic open
`X.basicOpen a` is a fraction `b / aᵏ` whose differential the Leibniz rule turns into a
combination of restrictions of `d b` and `d a` — that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.range_universalDSections_basicOpen_le_span`. Membership in the span
over `U` is then recovered from the basic opens by `Submodule.mem_of_isLocalized_span`,
`Ω_{X/S}` being quasi-coherent so that the span localizes. This is the same localization argument
as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.mem_of_cover`, which is not applied directly: its
hypothesis is the compatibility of a family, and for the family of spans of the ranges of `d` the
compatibility condition at an arbitrary nested pair of affine opens contains the statement being
proved.

The recursion this file's combination feeds is assembled in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.HomogeneousTwistCompatible`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FUH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FUH), clause (1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)

/-- **The differential of a function on a basic open of an affine open is a combination of
restrictions of the differentials of the functions on that affine open.** The function is a
fraction `b / t` with `b` and `t` functions on the affine open and `t` a power of the one cutting
out the basic open, where it is invertible; the Leibniz rule turns `t • d(b/t)` into
`d b - (b/t) • d t`, and dividing by the unit `t` is what the statement says. -/
theorem range_universalDSections_basicOpen_le_span {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    Set.range (universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)) ⊆
      Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)
        ((relativeDifferentials f).presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op ''
          Set.range (universalDSections f U)) := by
  have := hU.isLocalization_basicOpen a
  set Q := Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)
    ((relativeDifferentials f).presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op ''
      Set.range (universalDSections f U)) with hQ
  have hres : ∀ b : Γ(X, U), universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
      (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b) ∈ Q := fun b =>
    Submodule.subset_span ⟨universalDSections f U b, ⟨b, rfl⟩,
      ((universalRelativeDerivation f).d_map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op b).symm⟩
  rintro - ⟨c, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨b, t, rfl⟩ : ∃ (b : Γ(X, U)) (t : Submonoid.powers a),
      IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t = c := by
    obtain ⟨⟨b, t⟩, h⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective (Submonoid.powers a) c
    exact ⟨b, t, h⟩
  have hleib := (universalRelativeDerivation f).d_mul
    (IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t)
    (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) (t : Γ(X, U)))
  have hspec : IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t *
      algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) (t : Γ(X, U)) =
      algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b :=
    IsLocalization.mk'_spec Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t
  have hsum : IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t •
        universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
          (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) (t : Γ(X, U))) +
      algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) (t : Γ(X, U)) •
        universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
          (IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t) =
      universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
        (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b) :=
    hleib.symm.trans (congrArg (fun z => universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a) z) hspec)
  have hmem : (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) (t : Γ(X, U))) •
      universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
        (IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t) ∈ Q := by
    rw [eq_sub_of_add_eq' hsum]
    exact Submodule.sub_mem Q (hres b)
      (Submodule.smul_mem Q _ (hres (t : Γ(X, U))))
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := IsLocalization.map_units (M := Submonoid.powers a)
    Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) t
  have hunit : universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
        (IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t) =
      ((u⁻¹ : Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)ˣ) : Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)) •
        ((u : Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)) • universalDSections f (X.basicOpen a)
          (IsLocalization.mk' Γ(X, X.basicOpen a) b t)) := by
    rw [smul_smul, u.inv_mul, one_smul]
  rw [hunit, hu]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem Q _ hmem

/-- **The sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an affine open of `X` are generated over `Γ(X, U)` by the
relative de Rham differentials of the functions there**, with no hypothesis relating `U` to an
affine open of `S`. The affine open is covered by basic opens which *do* map into an affine open
of `S`; over each of those the differentials of the functions generate by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top`, and those functions are
fractions of functions on `U` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.range_universalDSections_basicOpen_le_span`. Membership in the
span is then recovered from the basic opens because `Ω_{X/S}` is quasi-coherent, so the span
localizes. -/
theorem span_range_universalDSections_eq_top_of_isAffineOpen {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Submodule.span Γ(X, U) (Set.range (universalDSections f U)) = ⊤ := by
  have : (relativeDifferentials f).IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_relativeDifferentials f
  set P := Submodule.span Γ(X, U) (Set.range (universalDSections f U)) with hP
  set s : Set Γ(X, U) := {a | ∃ V : S.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ X.basicOpen a ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V} with hs
  have hspan : Ideal.span s = ⊤ := by
    rw [← hU.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff]
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hzV, -⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp S.isBasis_affineOpens
      (show f.base z ∈ (⊤ : S.Opens) from trivial)
    obtain ⟨a, ha1, ha2⟩ := hU.exists_basicOpen_le
      (⟨z, show z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V from hzV⟩ : (f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) hz
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨a, V, hV, ha1⟩, ha2⟩
  refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.mpr fun x => ?_
  let _i₁ : ∀ r : s, Module Γ(X, U) Γ(relativeDifferentials f, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun r => moduleOfLE (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le _)
  let _i₃ : ∀ r : s, IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U)))
      Γ(relativeDifferentials f, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun r => isScalarTowerOfLE (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le _)
  let _i₄ : ∀ r : s, IsLocalization.Away (r : Γ(X, U)) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun r => hU.isLocalization_basicOpen _
  let _i₂ : ∀ r : s, IsLocalizedModule.Away (r : Γ(X, U))
      (restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))) :=
    fun r => isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) hU _ rfl _
  refine Submodule.mem_of_isLocalized_span s hspan
    (fun r => Γ(relativeDifferentials f, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U))))
    (fun r => restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))) fun r => ?_
  have key : Submodule.localized₀ (Submonoid.powers (r : Γ(X, U)))
        (restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))) P =
      (Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U)))
        (restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U))) ''
          (P : Set Γ(relativeDifferentials f, U)))).restrictScalars Γ(X, U) := by
    rw [← Submodule.restrictScalars_localized' Γ(X, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U))),
      Submodule.localized'_eq_span]
  rw [key, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem]
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVle⟩ := r.2
  have himg : (restrictₗ (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U))) ''
        (P : Set Γ(relativeDifferentials f, U))) =
      (relativeDifferentials f).presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))).op ''
        (P : Set Γ(relativeDifferentials f, U)) := rfl
  have htop : Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen (r : Γ(X, U)))
      ((relativeDifferentials f).presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))).op ''
        Set.range (universalDSections f U)) = ⊤ := by
    refine top_le_iff.mp ?_
    rw [← span_range_universalDSections_eq_top f (hU.basicOpen _) hV hVle]
    exact Submodule.span_le.mpr (range_universalDSections_basicOpen_le_span f hU _)
  rw [himg, span_image_span (relativeDifferentials f) (X.basicOpen_le (r : Γ(X, U)))
    (Set.range (universalDSections f U)), htop]
  trivial

/-- **Over a nested pair of affine charts the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over the smaller one are
spanned by the restrictions of the differentials of the functions on the bigger one.** The
differentials of the functions on the bigger chart span there, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top`, and the restrictions of the
sections over the bigger chart span over the smaller one, `Ω_{X/S}` being quasi-coherent; the two
compose because restricting a span and spanning again is spanning the restricted generators. -/
theorem span_image_range_universalDSections_eq_top {U W : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hWU : W ≤ U) :
    Submodule.span Γ(X, W)
        ((relativeDifferentials f).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op ''
          Set.range (universalDSections f U)) = ⊤ := by
  have : (relativeDifferentials f).IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_relativeDifferentials f
  rw [← Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.span_image_span (relativeDifferentials f) hWU
      (Set.range (universalDSections f U)),
    span_range_universalDSections_eq_top_of_isAffineOpen f hU, Submodule.top_coe,
    Set.image_univ]
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.span_range_restrict_eq_top
    (relativeDifferentials f) hU hW hWU

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace Stacks.LineBundle

variable (D : Situation.{u})

/-! ### The differential of a pulled-back function -/

/-- The square the canonical map of Tag 01UV is attached to: the projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X` followed by
`f` is the structure morphism `L^⋆ ⟶ S`. -/
theorem Situation.laurentSpectrumToBase_comp_f :
    D.laurentSpectrumToBase ≫ D.f = D.laurentToBase ≫ 𝟙 D.S := by
  rw [Category.comp_id]
  rfl

/-- **The adjoint of the canonical map of Tag 01UV at the projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X`**:
`Ω_{X/S} ⟶ π_* Ω_{L^⋆/S}`, a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules. Its transpose across the
pullback-pushforward adjunction is the map
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialsMap` of the square above. -/
def Situation.laurentDifferentialsPushHom :
    Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.f ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj
        (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction D.laurentSpectrumToBase).homEquiv _ _
    (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialsMap D.laurentSpectrumToBase D.f D.laurentToBase (𝟙 D.S)
      D.laurentSpectrumToBase_comp_f)

/-- **The adjoint carries the differential of a function on `X` to the differential of its
pullback to `L^⋆`.** -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferentialsPushHom_d (U : D.X.Opens) (a : Γ(D.X, U)) :
    (D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom.val.app (op U)).hom
        (Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f U a) =
      Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.laurentToBase (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U)
        ((D.laurentSpectrumToBase.app U).hom a) :=
  Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialsMap_app_d (𝟙 D.S) D.laurentSpectrumToBase_comp_f U a

/-- **The differential of a function pulled back from the smaller chart is a
`Γ(X, W)`-combination of restrictions of differentials of functions pulled back from the bigger
one.** The combination is found on `X`, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_image_range_universalDSections_eq_top` supplies it, and pushed
along the adjoint, which is a morphism of sheaves and so commutes with the restrictions. -/
theorem Situation.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span (U W : D.X.affineOpens)
    (hWU : W.1 ≤ U.1) (r : Γ(D.X, W.1)) :
    Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom W.1
        (Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f W.1 r) ∈
      Submodule.span Γ(D.X, W.1)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj
            (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase)).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op ''
          Set.range (fun a : Γ(D.X, U.1) =>
            Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom U.1
              (Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f U.1 a))) := by
  have hmem : Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f W.1 r ∈ Submodule.span Γ(D.X, W.1)
      ((Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.f).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op ''
        Set.range (Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f U.1)) := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.span_image_range_universalDSections_eq_top D.f U.2 W.2 hWU]
    trivial
  refine (Submodule.map_span_le (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom W.1)
    _ _).mpr ?_ (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem hmem)
  rintro - ⟨y, ⟨a, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  exact (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom.val
    (homOfLE hWU).op _).symm

/-! ### The pushforward re-seated where a compatible family can be stated -/

/-- **The pushed-forward relative forms of `L^⋆` at the `X.Modules` spelling.** This is
`Situation.laurentFormsPushforward` with its type given as `D.X.Modules`, which it is by
definition; see this file's implementation notes for why the spelling matters. -/
def Situation.gradedAmbient (p : ℕ) : D.X.Modules := D.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ)

/-- The homogeneous relative forms of degree `n` over an affine open of `X`, as a set of sections
of `Situation.gradedAmbient`. This is the generating family a compatible family of submodules
would be spanned by. -/
def Situation.homogeneousSet (p : ℕ) (n : ℤ) (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    Set Γ(D.gradedAmbient p, U.1) := {ω | D.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm U p n ω}

/-- **The restriction map of the re-seated pushforward is the inverse-image restriction of the
forms**, on the nose. This is what makes `Situation.isHomogeneousLaurentForm_map`, which is
stated at the forms' own spelling, usable about `Situation.gradedAmbient` with no bridging. -/
theorem Situation.gradedAmbient_presheaf_map (p : ℕ) {U W : D.X.affineOpens} (hWU : W.1 ≤ U.1)
    (ω : Γ(D.gradedAmbient p, U.1)) :
    (D.gradedAmbient p).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op ω =
      (D.laurentFormsAlgebra.piece (p : ℤ)).val.map (D.laurentPreimageHom hWU).op ω :=
  rfl

/-- **Restrictions of homogeneous forms of degree `n` are homogeneous of degree `n`.** -/
theorem Situation.homogeneousSet_image_subset (p : ℕ) (n : ℤ) {U W : D.X.affineOpens}
    (hWU : W.1 ≤ U.1) :
    (D.gradedAmbient p).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op '' D.homogeneousSet p n U ⊆
      D.homogeneousSet p n W := by
  rintro ω ⟨η, hη, rfl⟩
  exact D.isHomogeneousLaurentForm_map hWU p n η hη

/-- **One of the two inclusions a compatible family of submodules asks for**: the span of the
restrictions of the homogeneous forms over the bigger affine open is contained in the span of the
homogeneous forms over the smaller one. -/
theorem Situation.span_homogeneousSet_image_le (p : ℕ) (n : ℤ) {U W : D.X.affineOpens}
    (hWU : W.1 ≤ U.1) :
    Submodule.span Γ(D.X, W.1)
        ((D.gradedAmbient p).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op '' D.homogeneousSet p n U) ≤
      Submodule.span Γ(D.X, W.1) (D.homogeneousSet p n W) :=
  Submodule.span_mono (D.homogeneousSet_image_subset p n hWU)

/-! ### The pulled-back differential as a one-form -/

/-- **The degree-one generator of the exterior algebra of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}`, pushed forward to `X`**:
`π_* Ω_{L^⋆/S} ⟶ π_* Ω^1_{L^⋆/S}`, a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules. Reading the generator this way
is what makes it `Γ(X, W)`-linear on sections and natural in the open of `X`, which is what
carrying a `Γ(X, W)`-span along it asks for. -/
def Situation.laurentGeneratorPush :
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj
        (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase) ⟶ D.gradedAmbient 1 :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).map
    (Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase))

/-- **The adjoint of Tag 01UV followed by the pushed-forward generator is the relative de Rham
differential of the pulled-back function.** The left-hand side is where
`Situation.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span` puts its elements, and the right-hand side is the
spelling `Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm` is written in. -/
theorem Situation.laurentGeneratorPush_pushHom (U : D.X.Opens) (r : Γ(D.X, U)) :
    Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentGeneratorPush U
        (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom U
          (Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.f U r)) =
      (D.laurentDifferential (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U)
        (D.laurentPullbackFunction U r) : Γ(D.gradedAmbient 1, U)) :=
  (congrArg (D.laurentGeneratorSections (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      (D.laurentDifferentialsPushHom_d U r)).trans
    (D.laurentDifferential_eq_generatorSections (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U)
      (D.laurentPullbackFunction U r)).symm

/-- **The relative de Rham differential of a function pulled back from the smaller chart is a
`Γ(X, W)`-combination of restrictions of the differentials of functions pulled back from the
bigger one**, as a one-form on `L^⋆`. This is
`Situation.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span` carried along the pushed-forward degree-one
generator of the exterior algebra, which is `Γ(X, W)`-linear and commutes with restriction. -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferential_pullback_mem_span (U W : D.X.affineOpens)
    (hWU : W.1 ≤ U.1) (r : Γ(D.X, W.1)) :
    (D.laurentDifferential (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ W.1)
        (D.laurentPullbackFunction W.1 r) : Γ(D.gradedAmbient 1, W.1)) ∈
      Submodule.span Γ(D.X, W.1)
        ((D.gradedAmbient 1).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op ''
          Set.range fun a : Γ(D.X, U.1) =>
            (D.laurentDifferential (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
              (D.laurentPullbackFunction U.1 a) : Γ(D.gradedAmbient 1, U.1))) := by
  rw [← D.laurentGeneratorPush_pushHom W.1 r]
  refine (Submodule.map_span_le (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap D.laurentGeneratorPush W.1)
    _ _).mpr ?_ (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (D.laurentPushDifferential_mem_span U W hWU r))
  rintro - ⟨y, ⟨a, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  exact (congrArg ((D.gradedAmbient 1).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op)
      (D.laurentGeneratorPush_pushHom U.1 a)).symm.trans
    (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply D.laurentGeneratorPush.val (homOfLE hWU).op _).symm

end Stacks.LineBundle

end
